#: src/build-system-reference.md:30
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:32
msgid "`$ARCH` is the environment variable for a CPU architecture directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:33
msgid "`$BOARD` is the environment variable for a board model directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:34
msgid "`$TARGET` is the environment variable for CPU-specific recipe binaries"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:36
msgid "Build System Organization"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:38
msgid "Root directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:40
msgid "`podman_bootstrap.sh` - The script used to configure the Podman build"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:41
msgid "`native_bootstrap.sh` - The script used to configure the Native build"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:42
msgid ""
"`Makefile` - The main Makefile of the build system, it loads all the other "
"Makefiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:43
msgid ""
"`.config` - Where you override your build system settings. It is loaded by "
"the Makefile (it is ignored by `git`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:45
msgid "GNU Make Configuration"
msgstr "GNU Make 組態"

#: src/build-system-reference.md:47
msgid ""
"`mk/config.mk` - The build system settings are here. You can override these "
"settings in your `.config`, don't change them here to avoid conflicts in the "
"`make pull` command."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:48
msgid ""
"`mk/*.mk` - The rest of the Makefiles. You should not need to change them."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:50
msgid "Podman Configuration"
msgstr "Podman 組態"

#: src/build-system-reference.md:52
msgid ""
"`podman/redox-base-containerfile` - The file used to create the image used "
"by the Podman build. The installation of packages needed for the build is "
"done here. See the [Adding Packages to the Build](./advanced-podman-build."
"md#adding-packages-to-the-build) section if you need to add additional "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:54
msgid "Filesystem Configuration"
msgstr "檔案系統組態"

#: src/build-system-reference.md:56
msgid "`config` - This directory contains all filesystem configurations."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:57
msgid ""
"`config/*.toml` - Filesystem configurations (a template can use other "
"template to reduce duplication)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:58
msgid "`config/base.toml` - Essential configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:59
msgid ""
"`config/minimal.toml` - The variant without server tools and Orbital. Aimed "
"for low-end computers, embedded hardware, testers and developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:60
msgid ""
"`config/server.toml` - The variant with some important tools without "
"Orbital. Aimed for servers, low-end computers, testers and developers (try "
"this config if you have boot problems on QEMU or real hardware)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:61
msgid ""
"`config/$ARCH/server-demo.toml` - Configuration with for server demonstration"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:62
msgid ""
"`config/desktop-minimal.toml` - The minimal `desktop` variant for low-end "
"computers and embedded hardware. Aimed for servers, low-end computers, "
"embedded hardware and developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:63
msgid ""
"`config/desktop.toml` - The variant with some important CLI and GUI programs "
"(this is the default configuration of the build system). Aimed for end-"
"users, gamers, testers and developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:64
msgid ""
"`config/$ARCH/desktop-contain.toml` - `desktop` variant with sandbox enabled "
"by default"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:65
msgid ""
"`config/dev.toml` - The variant with development tools included. Aimed for "
"developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:66
msgid ""
"`config/demo.toml` - The variant with a complete system and optional "
"programs and games. Aimed for end-users, gamers, testers and developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:67
msgid "`config/x11.toml` - Configuration for X11 sessions and applications"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:68
msgid ""
"`config/wayland.toml` - Configuration for Wayland sessions and applications"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:69
msgid ""
"`config/acid.toml` - Configuration with the `acid` Redox test suite. Aimed "
"for developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:70
msgid "`config/os-test.toml` - Configuration with the `os-test` test suite"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:71
msgid ""
"`config/auto-test.toml` - Configuration with automated test suites execution"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:72
msgid ""
"`config/sys-build.toml` - Configuration with automated system compilation "
"testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:73
msgid "`config/tests.toml` - Configuration for tests"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:74
msgid "`config/redoxer.toml` - Configuration used to create the Redoxer image"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:75
msgid ""
"`config/redoxer-gui.toml` - Configuration used to create the Redoxer GUI "
"image"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:76
msgid ""
"`config/aarch64/$BOARD/*.toml` - ARM64 board model specific configurations"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:77
msgid ""
"`config/riscv64gc/$BOARD/*.toml` - RISC-V board model specific configurations"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:78
msgid "`config/$ARCH/redoxer.toml` - CPU-specific Redoxer configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:79
msgid ""
"`config/$ARCH/full.toml` - Configuration with all recipes enabled in the "
"package server"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:80
msgid ""
"`config/$ARCH/ci.toml` - Package server configuration, recipes added here "
"become packages on the [build server](https://static.redox-os.org/pkg/). "
"Aimed for packagers and developers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:81
msgid ""
"`config/$ARCH/jeremy.toml` - The configuration of [Jeremy Soller](https://"
"soller.dev/) (creator/BDFL of Redox) with the recipes that he is testing in "
"the moment."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:83
msgid "Build System Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:85
msgid ""
"`build` - The directory where the build system will place the final image. "
"Usually `build/$(ARCH)/$(CONFIG_NAME)`, e.g. `build/x86_64/desktop`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:86
msgid ""
"`build/$ARCH/your-config/harddrive.img` - The Redox image file, to be used "
"by QEMU or VirtualBox for virtual machine execution on a Unix-like host."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:87
msgid ""
"`build/$ARCH/your-config/redox-live.iso` - The Redox bootable image file, to "
"be used on real hardware for testing and possible installation."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:88
msgid ""
"`build/$ARCH/your-config/fetch.tag` - An empty file that, if present, tells "
"the build system that the downloading of recipe sources is done."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:89
msgid ""
"`build/$ARCH/your-config/repo.tag` - An empty file that, if present, tells "
"the build system that all recipes required for the Redox image have been "
"successfully built. **The build system will not check for changes to your "
"code when this file is present.** Use `make rebuild` to force the build "
"system to check for changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:90
msgid ""
"`build/podman` - The directory where Podman Build places the container "
"user's home directory, including the container's Rust installation. Use "
"`make container_clean` to remove it. In some situations, you may need to "
"remove this directory manually, possibly with root privileges."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:91
msgid ""
"`build/container.tag` - An empty file, created during the first Podman "
"build, so a Podman build knows when a reusable Podman image is available. "
"Use `make container_clean` to force a rebuild of the Podman image on your "
"next `make rebuild` run."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:92
msgid "`build/logs/$TARGET/recipe.log` - Where recipe build logs are stored."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:94
msgid "Cookbook"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:96
msgid ""
"`prefix/*` - Tools used by the Cookbook system. They are normally downloaded "
"during the first system build (if you are having a problem with the build "
"system, you can remove the `prefix` directory and it will be recreated "
"during the next build)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:97
msgid "`repo` - Contains all packaged recipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:98
msgid "`web` - Contains optional generated web content for `repo`."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:99
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe` - A recipe (software port) directory (represented as "
"`recipe`), this directory holds the `recipe.toml` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:100
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/recipe.toml` - The recipe configuration file, this "
"configuration contains instructions for downloading Git repositories or "
"tarballs, then creating executables or other files to include in the Redox "
"filesystem. Note that a recipe can contain dependencies that cause other "
"recipes to be built, even if the dependencies are not otherwise part of your "
"Redox build."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:102
msgid ""
"(To learn more about the recipe system read the [Porting Applications using "
"Recipes](./porting-applications.md) page)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:104
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/recipe.sh` - The old recipe configuration format (can't be "
"used as dependency of a recipe with a TOML syntax)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:105
msgid "`recipes/recipe/source.tar` - The tarball of the recipe (renamed)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:106
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/source` - The directory where the recipe source is extracted "
"or downloaded."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:107
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target` - The directory where the recipe binaries are stored."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:108
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}` - The directory for the recipe's binaries "
"of the CPU architecture."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:109
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}/build` - The directory where the recipe "
"build system runs its commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:110
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}/stage` - The directory where recipe "
"binaries go before the packaging, after `make all`, `make rebuild` and `make "
"image` the [installer](https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/installer) will "
"extract the recipe package on the QEMU image, generally at `/usr/bin` or `/"
"usr/lib` in a Redox filesystem hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:111
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}/sysroot` - The directory where recipe build "
"dependencies (libraries) are shared, for example: `*.so`, `*.a` and `cmake` "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:112
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}/toolchain` - The directory where recipe "
"tool dependencies (toolchain) are shared, for example: binaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:113
msgid "`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}/stage.pkgar` - Redox package file."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:114
msgid ""
"`recipes/recipe/target/${TARGET}/stage.toml` - Contains the runtime "
"dependencies of the package and is part of both package formats."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:116
msgid "GNU Make Commands"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:118
msgid ""
"You can combine `make` commands, but order is significant. For example, "
"`make r.games image` will build the `games` recipe and create a new Redox "
"image, but `make image r.games` will make the Redox image before the recipe "
"building, thus the new recipe binary will not be included on your Redox "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:120
msgid "Build System"
msgstr "建置系統"

#: src/build-system-reference.md:122
msgid ""
"`make pull` - Update the source code of the build system without building."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:123
msgid ""
"`make cookbook` - Update Cookbook binaries with local changes (when `make "
"pull` is not used)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:124
msgid ""
"`make all` - Builds the entire system, checking for changes and only "
"building as required. Only use this for the first build. If the system was "
"successfully built previously, this command may report `Nothing to be done "
"for 'all'`, even if some recipes have changed. Use `make rebuild` instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:125
msgid ""
"`make rebuild` - Update all binaries from recipes with source code changes "
"(it doesn't detect changes on the Redox toolchain). This should be your "
"normal `make` target."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:126
msgid ""
"`make rebuild-push` - Similar to `make rebuild` but push updated recipes "
"instead of a image rebuild, use this to preserve your changes on the Redox "
"image after a full update (it will update downloaded packages if "
"`REPO_BINARY` is enabled)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:127
msgid "`make prefix` - Download the Rust/GCC forks and build relibc."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:128
msgid ""
"`make fstools` - Build the Redox image builder (installer), Cookbook and "
"RedoxFS."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:129
msgid ""
"`make fstools_clean` - Clean the image builder, Cookbook and RedoxFS "
"binaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:130
msgid ""
"`make fetch` - Update recipe sources, according to each recipe, without "
"building them. Only the recipes that are included in your `(CONFIG_NAME)."
"toml` are downloaded. Does nothing if `$(BUILD)/fetch.tag` is present. You "
"won't need this."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:131
msgid "`make unfetch` - Clean all recipe sources."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:132
msgid ""
"`make cook` - Build recipes enabled in the active filesystem configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:133
msgid ""
"`make repo` - Package the recipe binaries, according to each recipe. Does "
"nothing if `$(BUILD)/repo.tag` is present. You won't need this."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:134
msgid "`make repo_clean` - Clean all recipe binaries"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:135
msgid ""
"`make repo_clean_target` - Clean all recipe binaries compiled to the active "
"CPU architecture (`ARCH=value` environment variable)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:136
msgid ""
"`make repo-lock` - Lock the commit hashes of recipe sources using a Git "
"repositories"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:137
msgid ""
"`make repo-unlock` - Unlock the commit hashes of recipe sources using a Git "
"repositories"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:138
msgid ""
"`make repo-rollback` - Return to a specific Cookbook commit hash for "
"debugging, don't work with commits from before 2026"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:139
msgid ""
"`make clean` - Clean all recipe binaries and packages (Note that `make "
"clean` may require some tools to be built)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:140
msgid "`make static_clean` - Clean all statically linked recipe binaries"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:141
msgid ""
"`make distclean` - Clean all recipe sources, binaries, and packages "
"(**please backup or submit your source changes before the execution of this "
"command**)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:142
msgid "`make find` - Show the recipe packages location"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:143
msgid ""
"`make tree` - Show all recipe and package dependencies from the current "
"filesystem configuration that will be built and pushed"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:144
msgid ""
"`make repo-tree` - Show all recipe dependencies (`build.dependencies` data "
"type) that will be built, also check what dependencies were built or not"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:145
msgid ""
"`make image-tree` - Show the package dependencies (`package.dependencies` "
"data type) that will be pushed into the Redox image"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:146
msgid ""
"`make image` - Builds a new QEMU image, `build/harddrive.img`, without "
"checking if any recipes have changed. It can save you some time if you are "
"just updating one recipe with `make r.recipe`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:147
msgid ""
"`make push` - Only install recipes with new changes in an existing Redox "
"image (it can still be used after `make c.--all` or `make u.--all` execution)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:148
msgid ""
"`make install` - Install the recipe binaries in the system for self-hosted "
"development testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:149
msgid ""
"`make mount` - Mounts the Redox image as a filesystem at `$(BUILD)/"
"filesystem`. **Do not use this if QEMU is running**, and remember to use "
"`make unmount` as soon as you are done. This is not recommended, but if you "
"need to get a large file onto or off of your Redox image, this is available "
"as a workaround."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:150
msgid ""
"`make unmount` - Unmounts the Redox image filesystem. Use this as soon as "
"you are done with `make mount`, and **do not start QEMU** until this is done."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:151
msgid ""
"`make live` - Creates a bootable image, `build/livedisk.iso`. Recipes are "
"not usually rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:152
msgid ""
"`make popsicle` - Flash the Redox bootable image on your USB device using "
"the [Popsicle](https://github.com/pop-os/popsicle) tool (the program "
"executable must be present on your shell `$PATH` environment variable, you "
"can get the executable by extracting the AppImage, installing from the "
"package manager or building from source)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:153
msgid "`make mount_live` - Mount the live disk ISO"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:154
msgid ""
"`make env` - Creates a shell with a build environment configured to use the "
"Redox toolchain. If you are using Podman Build it will change your current "
"terminal shell to the container shell, you can use it to update crates of "
"Rust programs or debug build issues such as missing packages (if you are "
"using the Podman Build you can only use this command in one terminal shell, "
"because it will block the build system directory access from other Podman "
"shell)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:156
msgid "Podman"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:158
msgid ""
"`make container_shell` - Open the GNU Bash shell of the Podman container as "
"the active shell of your terminal, it's logged as the `podman` user without "
"`root` privileges (don't use this command to replace the `make env` command "
"because it don't setup the Redox toolchain in the Podman container shell)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:159
msgid ""
"`make container_clean` - This will discard images and other files created by "
"Podman."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:160
msgid ""
"`make container_touch` - If you have removed the file `build/container.tag`, "
"but the container image is still usable, this will recreate the `container."
"tag` file and avoid rebuilding the container image."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:161
msgid ""
"`make container_kill` - If you have started a build using Podman Build, and "
"you want to stop it, `Ctrl-C` may not be sufficient. Use this command to "
"terminate the most recently created container."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:163
msgid "Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:165
msgid "(The `recipe` in `make x.recipe` is the recipe directory name)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:167
msgid ""
"`make f.recipe` (abbreviation of `fetch`) - Download one or multiple recipe "
"sources"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:168
msgid ""
"`make r.recipe` (abbreviation of `repo`) - Build one or multiple recipes, "
"checking if the recipe source has changed, and creating the executable, etc. "
"e.g. `make r.games` (you can't use this command to replace the `make all`, "
"`make fstools` and `make prefix` commands because it don't trigger them, "
"make sure to run them before to avoid errors)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:170
msgid ""
"Meta-packages need the `--with-package-deps` option, for example: `make r."
"meta-package,--with-package-deps`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:171
msgid "The recipe is built even if it's not in your filesystem configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:172
msgid ""
"This command will continue where you stopped the build process, it's useful "
"to save time if you had a compilation error and patched a crate"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:174
msgid "`make ri.recipe` - Build or rebuild and install the recipe to Redox"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:175
msgid ""
"`make p.recipe` (abbreviation of `push`) - Install one or multiple recipe "
"packages to an existing Redox image (it can still be used after `make c."
"recipe` or `make u.recipe` execution)"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:176
msgid ""
"`make i.recipe` (abbreviation of `install`) - Install a recipe to Redox for "
"self-hosted development testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:177
msgid ""
