msgid "`make x.--category` - Run any recipe target (x) in all recipes"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:210
msgid ""
"`make x.--category-directory-name` - Run any recipe target (x) in all "
"recipes of some category directory at `recipes` (like `make u.--category-"
"wip` which clean all recipe sources and binaries from the `wip` directory, "
"for example), if you need to use a sub-category use `--category-directory-"
"name/subdirectory`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:212
msgid ""
"All recipe targets also support multiple recipe entries by separating each "
"recipe name with a comma. for example: `make f.recipe1,recipe2` will "
"download the sources of `recipe1` and `recipe2`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:214
msgid "QEMU/VirtualBox"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:216
msgid ""
"`make qemu` - Boot Redox in QEMU, if a `build/harddrive.img` file exists "
"QEMU will run using that image. If you want to force a rebuild first, run "
"the `make rebuild qemu` command. Sometimes `make qemu` will detect changes "
"and rebuild, but this is not typical. If you are interested in a particular "
"combination of QEMU command line options, have a look through `mk/qemu.mk`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:217
msgid "`make qemu gpu=no` - Start QEMU without a GUI (disables Orbital)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:218
msgid "`make qemu gpu=virtio` - Start QEMU with the VirtIO GPU driver."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:219
msgid "`make qemu audio=no` - Disable all sound drivers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:220
msgid "`make qemu usb=no` - Disable all USB drivers."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:221
msgid ""
"`make qemu uefi=yes` - Enable the UEFI boot loader (it supports more screen "
"resolutions)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:222
msgid "`make qemu live=yes` - Fully load the Redox image to RAM."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:223
msgid ""
"`make qemu disk=nvme` - Boot Redox from a NVMe interface (high-performance "
"SSD emulation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:224
msgid "`make qemu disk=usb` - Boot Redox from a virtual USB device."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:225
msgid "`make qemu disk=cdrom` - Boot Redox from a virtual CD-ROM disk."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:226
msgid ""
"`make qemu kvm=no` - Start QEMU without the [Linux KVM](https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Kernel-based_Virtual_Machine) acceleration if it's not supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:227
msgid ""
"`make qemu iommu=yes` - Start QEMU with [IOMMU](https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/Input-output_memory_management_unit) enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:228
msgid ""
"`make qemu gdb=yes` - Start QEMU with the GDB configuration enabled, you "
"need to run the `make rp.gdbserver` command before to install the GDB server "
"in the Redox image (persist until the next image creation) or add the "
"`gdbserver` recipe on your filesystem configuration (`gdbserver = {}`) to "
"persist in new images, then run the `make gdb` command in another shell to "
"connect the GDB processes."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:229
msgid ""
"`make gdb` - Connects the host system GDB to the GDB server (`gdbserver` "
"recipe) running inside of Redox in QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:230
msgid ""
"`make qemu option1=value option2=value` - Cumulative QEMU options are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:231
msgid ""
"`make virtualbox` - Boot Redox in VirtualBox, it requires the VirtualBox "
"service to be running, run `systemctl status vboxdrv.service` to verify or "
"`akmods; systemctl restart vboxdrv.service` to enable on systems using "
"systemd."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:233
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:235
msgid "`$(BUILD)` - Represents the `build` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:236
msgid "`$(ARCH)` - Represents the CPU architecture directory at `build`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:237
msgid ""
"`${TARGET}` - Represents the CPU architecture directory at the `recipes/"
"recipe/target` directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:238
msgid ""
"`$(CONFIG_NAME)` - Represents your filesystem configuration directory at "
"`build/$ARCH`"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:240
msgid ""
"We recommend that you use these variables with the `\"` symbol to clean any "
"spaces on the path, spaces are interpreted as command separators and will "
"break the commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:242
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:244
msgid ""
"```\n"
"\"${VARIABLE_NAME}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:248
msgid ""
"If you have a directory inside the variable directory you can call it with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:250
msgid ""
"```\n"
"\"${VARIABLE_NAME}\"/directory-name\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:254
msgid "Or"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:256
msgid ""
"```\n"
"\"${VARIABLE_NAME}/directory-name\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:260
msgid "Git Auto-checkout"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:262
msgid ""
"The `make rebuild` and `make r.recipe` commands will Git checkout (change "
"the active branch) of the recipe source to `master` (only recipes that fetch "
"Git repositories are affected, thus all Redox components)."
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:264
msgid ""
"If you are working in a separated branch on the recipe source and want to "
"disable this, change the type of your recipe on your filesystem "
"configuration :"
msgstr ""

#: src/build-system-reference.md:266
msgid ""
"```\n"
"[packages]\n"
"...\n"
"your-recipe = \"local\"\n"
"...\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

